PostgreSQL Jobs And Scheduling Plan
===================================

Goal
----
Add a PostgreSQL job/scheduling workflow comparable to pgAdmin's pgAgent integration, if the team wants PostgreSQL admin coverage beyond querying and browsing.

Scope
-----
- pgAgent-oriented visibility and management
- basic job list / inspect / create flows

Non-Goals
---------
- No homegrown scheduler in v1
- No cross-engine background job system

Reality Check
-------------
This plan is lower-priority than backup, shell, maintenance, and pgvector.
It should only move forward if PostgreSQL admin parity is a real product goal.

Implementation Outline
----------------------
Step 1: Capability detection
- Detect whether pgAgent is installed and reachable.

Verify:
- The feature stays hidden when pgAgent is not present.

Step 2: Read-only visibility
- Start with listing jobs and job steps before allowing writes.

Verify:
- Users can inspect existing jobs safely.

Step 3: Create/edit workflow
- Add a guided UI for common job definitions if read-only visibility proves useful.

Verify:
- Job creation maps cleanly to pgAgent concepts without inventing parallel abstractions.

Open Questions
--------------
- Is pgAgent common enough among target users to justify the complexity?
- Should this remain read-only indefinitely?

MVP Recommendation
------------------
Do not prioritize this until higher-value PostgreSQL gaps are closed.
